      "writtenOn": "2025-11-24T19:12:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "since the goal is to get certain bots to always run on certain changes, it seems like configuring those bots to run on those changes would be the best approach, i.e. https://chromium.googlesource.com/infra/luci/luci-go/+/HEAD/lucicfg/doc/README.md#filtering-based-on-files-touched-by-a-cl",
      "revId": "32f9499c6b995b1cdfb9e6cd6ea5cb2082279530",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5d4678b0_7c38e46f",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1286337
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-11-24T19:28:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is something we\u0027ve discussed extensively in b/433778690. The goal is to have a certain people always get a specific bot added - there is no configuration I\u0027m aware of that can accomplish this right now (without also turning off the ability for those outside the group to run it). This is a low lift solution which gets us most of the way there without needing to implement new stuff in LUCI.",
      "parentUuid": "76389e1c_dec746c0",
      "revId": "32f9499c6b995b1cdfb9e6cd6ea5cb2082279530",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "41383e07_b838a6ea",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1381059
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-11-24T22:02:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think in the long run, this should be expressed in the CQ configuration instead of complicating depot_tools further (You already noticed the caveat that the Cider G workflow is not supported with this proposed flow). I agree that nothing in the CQ configuration today can support your use case unless we make improvements on more flexible builder triggering condition. \n\nAs a temporary workaround, I\u0027m wondering if we could introduce a new property in the CQ configuration to allow you to bypass owners_whitelist check when Cq-Include-Trybots is specified. That way, you can define the builder with the owner_whitelist set to the group you are targeting but in the meantime, people outside the group can still use Cq-Include-Trybots footer to explicitly launch the builder. Alternatively, we could also introduce additional groups that can use Cq-Include-Trybots to trigger the builder in addition to the groups defined in owners_whitelist. I\u0027m happy to make either of those changes.",
      "parentUuid": "5d4678b0_7c38e46f",
      "revId": "32f9499c6b995b1cdfb9e6cd6ea5cb2082279530",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
